Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 02:24:37 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 1402/1463] HERESY 1447: a LoRA's wave and the budget its
 layers share, on the page

Each LoRA row a wave beside its strengths, the sliders' own picture and editor (Flat, Arch, Draw; points dragged, added, taken out), one wave for a pair's two files; Budget: Off, Share (past the red line each gives way in proportion), In order (the top row first, the rows dragged to order them); the groups the lab's (adapters that push on the same layers), the caps the measured red lines (music 2.25, sound 1.5). The request carries each lora's "curve" and "group" and the "lora_groups"; a take or a prompt brings them back; the draft keeps them. The lab's word in the row's tip (where it pushes: the layers, attention against MLP, how far it moves them) and in the notes (two that share their layers, and how they pull). A slider's note in the stage is its "at gain" line only, never its wave as it goes. Fifteen strings in the eleven languages.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
